      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ea6b679e-a5a4-5394-86ac-d72e1ad5e997",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lodoicea, Lodoicea maldivica, privet, Ligustrum, Ligustrum vulgare, Ligustrum ovalifolium\n- Places: Seychelles, Praslin, Curieuse, Europe, North Africa, Asia, Australasia, Queensland\n- Concepts: monotypic genus, palm family, flowering plants, privacy hedging\n\nFacts:\n- Lodoicea is a monotypic genus in the palm family and is commonly known as the sea coconut, coco de mer, or double coconut.\n- Lodoicea maldivica is the sole species in the genus Lodoicea and is endemic to Praslin and Curieuse in the Seychelles.\n- A privet is a flowering plant in the genus Ligustrum.\n- The genus Ligustrum contains about 50 species of erect deciduous or evergreen shrubs that sometimes form small or medium-sized trees.\n- Ligustrum species are native to Europe, North Africa, and Asia, and many have been introduced and naturalised in Australasia.\n- In Australasia, only one Ligustrum species extends as a native into Queensland.\n- The name privet originally referred to the European semi-evergreen shrub Ligustrum vulgare.\n- The name privet was later also used for Ligustrum ovalifolium, which was used extensively for privacy hedging, and it is now applied to all members of the genus Ligustrum.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "43becc27-45c1-5ea6-8e6c-62df00e6282d",
        "text": "Page: Lodoicea. Sentence: Lodoicea, commonly known as the sea coconut, coco de mer, or double coconut, is a monotypic genus in the palm family.\nPage: Lodoicea. Sentence: The sole species, Lodoicea maldivica, is endemic to the islands of Praslin and Curieuse in the Seychelles.\nPage: Privet. Sentence: A privet is a flowering plant in the genus Ligustrum.\nPage: Privet. Sentence: The genus contains about 50 species of erect, deciduous or evergreen shrubs, sometimes forming small or medium-sized trees, native to Europe, north Africa, Asia, many introduced and naturalised in Australasia, where only one species extends as a native into Queensland.\nPage: Privet. Sentence: \"Privet\" was originally the name for the European semi-evergreen shrub \"Ligustrum vulgare\", and later also for the more reliably evergreen \"Ligustrum ovalifolium\" used extensively for privacy hedging, though now the name is applied to all members of the genus.",
